{
  "category": "Psi Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Using its ability to read minds, it will identify impending danger and TELEPORT to safety.",
      "version": "red"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using its ability to read minds, it will identify impending danger and TELEPORT to safety.",
      "version": "blue"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sleeps 18 hours a day. If it senses danger, it will teleport itself to safety even as it sleeps.",
      "version": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "text": "It senses impending attacks and TELEPORTS away to safety before the actual attacks can strike.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "If it decides to TELEPORT randomly, it creates the illusion that it has created copies of itself.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "It hypnotizes itself so that it can teleport away when it senses danger, even if it is asleep.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "ABRA sleeps for eighteen hours a day. However, it can sense the presence of foes even while it is sleeping. In such a situation, this POKéMON immediately teleports to safety.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "ABRA needs to sleep for eighteen hours a day. If it doesn’t, this POKéMON loses its ability to use telekinetic powers. If it is attacked, ABRA escapes using TELEPORT while it is still sleeping.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "A POKéMON that sleeps 18 hours a day. Observation revealed that it uses TELEPORT to change its location once every hour.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "It sleeps for 18 hours a day. It uses a variety of extrasensory powers even while asleep.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using its ability to read minds, it will sense impending danger and TELEPORT to safety.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "It sleeps for 18 hours a day. Even when awake, it teleports itself while remaining seated.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "Even while asleep, it maintains a telepathic radar. It teleports when it is threatened.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using its psychic power is such a strain on its brain that it needs to sleep for 18 hours a day.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "It senses impending attacks and teleports away to safety before the actual attacks can strike.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "If it decides to teleport randomly, it evokes the illusion that it has created copies of itself.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using its psychic power is such a strain on its brain that it needs to sleep for 18 hours a day.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using its psychic power is such a strain on its brain that it needs to sleep for 18 hours a day.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using its psychic power is such a strain on its brain that it needs to sleep for 18 hours a day.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using its psychic power is such a strain on its brain that it needs to sleep for 18 hours a day.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "It sleeps for 18 hours a day. It uses a variety of extrasensory powers even while asleep.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "It senses impending attacks and teleports away to safety before the actual attacks can strike.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Abra sleeps for eighteen hours a day. However, it can sense the presence of foes even while it is sleeping. In such a situation, this Pokémon immediately teleports to safety.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Abra needs to sleep for eighteen hours a day. If it doesn’t, this Pokémon loses its ability to use telekinetic powers. If it is attacked, Abra escapes using Teleport while it is still sleeping.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It sleeps 18 hours a day. Even while sleeping, it will teleport itself to treetops and pick and eat berries there.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It can teleport itself to safety while it’s asleep, but when it wakes, it doesn’t know where it is, so it panics.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It uses various psychic powers even while it’s sleeping, so you can’t tell whether or not it’s awake.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It can read others’ minds and will teleport away when danger approaches. You must clear your mind if you want to catch it.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sleeps 18 hours a day. If it senses danger, it will teleport itself to safety even as it sleeps.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sleeps 18 hours a day. If it senses danger, it will teleport itself to safety even as it sleeps.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon uses its psychic powers while it sleeps. The contents of Abra’s dreams affect the powers that the Pokémon wields.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Abra can teleport in its sleep. Apparently the more deeply Abra sleeps, the farther its teleportations go.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "Spends 18 hours of the day sleeping. Even while asleep, Abra can control its psychic powers—should danger approach, the Pokémon will simply teleport away.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
